# CloudflareEdgeHost5xxRatio — the edge-5xx belt (2026-10-29), lifted VERBATIM out of
# prometheusrule.yaml (comments stripped, the manifest is their one home). This is the rules file
# that edge-5xx.promtool-test loads. Not a manifest and not applied to anything: `promtool test
# rules` needs upstream-format rules (top-level `groups:`), and a PrometheusRule keeps them under
# `.spec`, so the CR cannot be loaded directly. Named .promtool-rules rather than .yaml on purpose
# — manifest-lint kubeconforms EVERY *.yaml under argocd/resources and a non-manifest there would
# fail it.
#
# The FOURTH fixture pair in this directory (spend-belt #334, exporter-down #351, edge-belt #1306).
# A SEPARATE PAIR rather than a second rule in edge-belt.promtool-rules, for the reason
# exporter-down.promtool-rules records: promtool evaluates EVERY rule in EVERY loaded file at EVERY
# step of EVERY test in that file, so rules sharing a file must tolerate each other's inputs. These
# tests drive `cloudflare_edge_requests_total` counters through bursts, outages and resets that the
# edge-belt cases (which model `cloudflare_edge_probe_ok` only) have no business seeing.
#
# ⚠ NOT DRIFT-PINNED (homelab#337) — a stale hand copy tests the OLD expr and passes VACUOUSLY.
# Re-copy after every expr edit:
#
#   devbox run -- yq -o=json '{"groups": [{"name": "cloudflare-edge-5xx", "rules": [.spec.groups[].rules[] | select(.alert == "CloudflareEdgeHost5xxRatio")]}]}' argocd/resources/cloudflare-exporter/prometheusrule.yaml | devbox run -- yq -P '.'
#
# The OTHER checks in this directory do NOT see this alert: `devbox run edge-probe-self-test`
# replays only CloudflareEdgeProbeBlind (its one-instant evaluator cannot model `increase()` or a
# ratio), and manifest-lint SKIPS the CR outright (kubeconform has no PrometheusRule schema). For
# CloudflareEdgeHost5xxRatio, this fixture is the whole gate.
groups:
  - name: cloudflare-edge-5xx
    rules:
      - alert: CloudflareEdgeHost5xxRatio
        expr: (sum by (zone, host) (increase(cloudflare_edge_requests_total{status=~"5.."}[30m])) / sum by (zone, host) (increase(cloudflare_edge_requests_total[30m])) > 0.25) and (sum by (zone, host) (increase(cloudflare_edge_requests_total{status=~"5.."}[30m])) > 20)
        for: 15m
        labels:
          severity: warning
          triage: dig
        annotations:
          summary: 'Cloudflare edge: {{ $labels.host }} is answering {{ $value | humanizePercentage }} 5xx'
          description: 'More than a quarter of {{ $labels.host }}''s edge responses over 30m were 5xx (and more than 20 of them), for 15m — the Cloudflare edge is failing requests to this host. SYMPTOM ONLY: a 52x/530 with origin status 0 is the edge↔tunnel hop (connector dead, wedged QUIC connection, Cloudflare incident); an origin-generated 5xx shows in the origin''s own response counters. Check: the claim''s cloudflared pods + logs and cloudflared_tunnel_* in its namespace, the origin pods, then the GraphQL read of originResponseStatus by hour (docs/cloudflare.md §Observability). Sized so the 2026-10-28/29 trickle (≤13 edge 520s per 30m, ≤12 %) stays silent — that rate is not actionable.'
